# Voice performance: Story (2008) vowel [u] tract, fold card of the licensed two-mass pack, target note C3 (130.81 Hz).
# Every number below is cited. UNKNOWN marks a quantity no cited source gives; none is fitted to a recording.
#
# TRACT: Story, B. H. (2008). Comparison of magnetic resonance imaging-based vocal tract area functions obtained from the same speaker in 1994 and 2002. J. Acoust. Soc. Am. 123(1):327-335, doi:10.1121/1.2805683; author manuscript PMC2377017.
#   Table I column [u], sections 1-44 glottis to lips, in file order. Areas are the printed
#   cm^2 digits scaled by e-4 (to m^2); the section length is the printed Delta (cm) scaled by e-2 (to m):
#   Delta = 0.445 cm, VTL = 44 Delta = 19.59 cm. One male speaker, MRI of 2002, vowel sustained supine.
#   LIMIT: a speech configuration, not a singing posture (larynx height, pharynx and lip shape differ in singing).
#   Same-specimen oracle for the passive tract (Table II, same speaker, same vowel):
#     measured  F1N 430±5  F2N 917±14  F3N 2087±14 Hz; Fo 155 Hz
#     computed  F1C 314  F2C 702  F3C 2298 Hz (the paper's own model)
#
# FOLD: lower/upper mass 0.125 g / 0.025 g, k 80 / 8 N/m, coupling 25 N/m, fold length 1.4 cm, lower-mass
#   thickness 0.25 cm: Ishizaka & Flanagan (1972) two-mass set in the Steinecke & Herzel (1995) form, as carried by
#   the CC-BY model-card pack twomass-if72-standard-plos-pone0187486 (see crates/fs-couple/src/glottis.rs).
#   Rest half-gap 3.57e-4 m = Steinecke-Herzel rest area 0.05 cm^2 / 1.4 cm. Damping ratios 0.1 lower, 0.6 upper
#   open: Ishizaka & Flanagan (1972) p. 1238, their typical condition, and the law adds 1.0 to each while its own section
#   is shut (eq 3 and 4; per mass is the working reading, see glottis.rs). Collision law and mucosal delay are fixed in
#   glottis.rs. RETRIM on this law: only q moved, pressure held, emergent f0 to within 3 cents of the note, no recording, q 0.470604 to 0.918467.
#   Trace:
#     q 0.470604: f0 100.63 Hz (-454.2 c) -> q 0.752966: f0 122.76 Hz (-109.9 c) -> q 0.874938: f0 128.80 Hz (-26.9 c) ->
#     q 0.918467: f0 130.61 Hz (-2.6 c)
#   Any other trace in this header is from an earlier law and ended at an earlier q.
#   PITCH CONTROL (model-only objective): the three fold stiffnesses are the pack values x q = 0.918467. q was found by
#   rendering and measuring the EMERGENT f0 of the radiated pressure (autocorrelation over 0.5-1.5 s of a 1.5 s trial render, then
#   re-measured on the full 3 s render) and iterating q until it was
#   within 3 cents of the target note C3 = 130.81 Hz (equal temperament, A4 = 440 Hz). No recording enters. Trace on the
#   sibling description story2008-u-C3-r1 (this file reuses its fold card):
#     q 0.504353: f0 135.04 Hz (+55.1 c) -> q 0.473244: f0 131.15 Hz (+4.5 c) -> q 0.470604: f0 130.79 Hz (-0.3 c)
#   The first rule tried (set the isolated in-phase mode f = sqrt((k1+k2)/(m1+m2))/2pi to the note) phonated 550-815 cents
#   sharp: the pair oscillates nearer its second eigenmode (200.5 Hz at q = 1, pack values) than its in-phase mode (120.4 Hz).
#   Eigenmodes from det(K - w^2 M) = 0 with the pack masses, stiffnesses and coupling; tract loading then moves f0 by a
#   vowel-dependent amount, which is why q differs between vowels at the same note.
# SUBGLOTTAL PRESSURE: AUTHORED PLAYER INPUT, 423.544 Pa: 900 Pa x the q 0.470604 of the previous trim, held when q moved on this law, so no longer 900 Pa x the q above: the drive rule of the in-repo vowel gate,
#   tests/vowel_gates.rs vw-002, which scales the drive with the stiffness. UNKNOWN for the recorded speaker: Story (2008) reports none; a measured source
#   would be Holmberg, Hillman & Perkell (1988) subglottal pressures. Q1 sweeps it (voice_q1_subglottal_pressure_metamorphic).
#   Ramp 0 -> P over 60 ms, hold, ramp to 0 over the last 150 ms.
# GAS: saturated air at 310.15 K and 101325 Pa. UNKNOWN as a source: Story (2008) does not state the speed of sound
#   its calculation used; the value is the declared physiological state of tract air, not fitted.
# TERMINATION: flanged (the mouth modelled as a piston in an infinite baffle, matching the receiver below).
# WALL: none (rigid). UNKNOWN as a measurement: the yielding-wall impedance of this tract; the cited setting is in the -flanagan files.
#   The paper's calculation included yielding walls, so formant widths differ by this gap. A rigid wall also leaves the first formant
#   with a bandwidth below the 50-90 Hz measured for humans (Birkholz et al. 2022), which makes /u/ at and above F1 irregular.
#   Before the DC-bin fix 2e629d5f3 this REFUSED at the 96 kHz clock (mouth-flow ladder tail 1.08e-10 against 1e-10); the cause
#   was that defect, and it renders with binary da31fbd67ee9. At C4 it is irregular (R(T)/R(0) 0.85, 48 to 192 kHz clocks).
# MICROPHONE: 0.30 m from the mouth at 45 degrees off axis (x = z = 0.30 sin 45 deg), the geometry of the paper's
#   recordings (AKG CK92 at 30 cm, 45 degrees off axis). Infinite baffle: no head diffraction. 16 rings x 64 points,
#   8 kHz resolved band (quadrature admission: 2 pi f cell / c <= pi/4).
# LEVEL: full_scale_pa 8.0 Pa (112 dB SPL peak at the PCM ceiling) is a recording-level choice, the same for
#   every description so vowel levels compare; the loudest render (a-D4) peaks at 4.89 Pa. Output is never normalized.
# MECHANICS: 96 kHz physical clock (2 per output sample), read through the bandlimited differentiating receiver.
frankensim-voice-performance-v1
audio 48000 144000 2
full_scale_pa 8.0
ambient moist_air 310.15 101325 1.0
fold two_mass 0.000125 2.5e-05 73.4774 7.34774 22.9617 0.1 3.57e-4 1.4e-2 2.5e-3
fold_damping_upper 0.6
termination flanged
tract_source story-2008-jasa-123-327-table-I-u
tract_licence published measurements transcribed with citation (Story 2008 Table I); redistribution terms unconfirmed, owner to decide
